/**
 * HTTP driver for the OIDC Authorization Endpoint, handling the interactive HTML login flow.
 *
 * This class is responsible for presenting and processing the browser-facing authorization UI
 * that implements RFC 6749 / OpenID Connect Core. It covers three main concerns: initiating
 * the authorization flow (GET /authorize), processing each incremental login step submitted
 * by the user (POST /authorize), and resuming an already-active session without re-prompting
 * the user for credentials (check-session/refresh endpoint).
 *
 * The class resolves PAR (Pushed Authorization Request) URIs and signed request objects through
 * AuthorizationRequestResolver before building the flow context. A consumed PAR or JAR request is
 * replaced by a redirect to its signed reference (request_ref), because the step forms post back
 * to their own URL and the request_uri or request object cannot be used twice. It validates PKCE
 * challenges against the client's policy, delegates step rendering and
 * authentication to OidcStepRouter, and emits the final response with the authorization code
 * (and tokens for a hybrid response type) once all challenges have been satisfied. Errors go
 * back to the client through AuthorizationResponseWriter only once the redirect URI is validated
 * for the client; before that they are local. Cookies for both the pre-session state and the
 * authenticated session are managed via OidcCookieManager.
 *
 * Whether the browser session serves the request (prompt, max_age and the tenant's SSO lifetime)
 * is decided by SessionSufficiencyPolicy, both when the request arrives and again at
 * check-session, so posting there directly cannot skip it. prompt=consent shows the scope consent
 * screen again after the login or on top of the session, and prompt=none never shows any UI: it
 * fails with login_required, consent_required or interaction_required (task 031).
 *
 * Relationships: depends on AuthenticateUser (domain service), SessionManager, OidcStepRouter
 * (step dispatch), OidcResponseBuilder (successful response), AuthorizationResponseWriter (error
 * responses), HtmlSecurer (CSRF token verification), and DecorateHtml (themed page wrapping).
 */
class AuthorizeHtml
{
